REM ertabat — take one package from roadmap/packages.json to a proof
REM targets PANINI spec as published at zistgah/panini
CYCLER "ertabat"
TITLE "One package, one proof"
OUTPUT KIND LINK
RESOLUTION MID

STAGE CONCEPT
  VERB CREATE
  SHAPE TEXT
  ASK <<
    Name the package id you are taking, and state in one sentence what will be TRUE
    when it is done that is not true now.
    Then state what is physically present: the radio by model, the antenna, the cable,
    the computer. If nothing is present, say so — a package proven only against the
    mock is a real result, and calling it a hardware result is not.
  >>
  EXPECT TEXT
  VALIDATE "names one package id and the hardware present, or says none"
END STAGE

STAGE BOUNDS
  VERB MEASURE
  SHAPE JSON
  ASK <<
    Which conformance conditions does this package touch? For each, copy the criterion
    and its unit from conformance/conditions.json verbatim.
    If a condition you touch reads 'not established', you may not establish it by
    assumption. Either measure it in this package or leave it unjudged and say so.
    State the band and power if anything transmits, and the authorisation under which
    it may be used. No authorisation, no transmit.
  >>
  EXPECT JSON
END STAGE

STAGE IMPLEMENT
  VERB CREATE
  SHAPE TEXT
  ASK <<
    Write only inside the paths this package owns. Every interface function the
    substrate cannot perform returns the unsupported code.
    Do not touch another package's paths. If you find you need to, stop and say which
    package you actually have.
  >>
  EXPECT TEXT
END STAGE

STAGE EXECUTE
  VERB EXECUTE
  SHAPE TEXT
  ASK <<
    Run the package's acceptance commands, exactly as written in roadmap/packages.json.
    Paste the output verbatim, including failures.
    A command you did not run is reported as not run.
  >>
  EXPECT TEXT
END STAGE

STAGE MEASURE
  VERB MEASURE
  SHAPE DATA
  ASK <<
    Attach the captured measurement: instrument, timestamp, method, raw values.
    If you are about to write a comparative word — faster, better, optimal — give the
    two numbers it compares. Without both numbers, delete the word.
  >>
  EXPECT DATA
END STAGE

STAGE FALSIFY
  VERB FALSIFY
  SHAPE TEXT
  ASK <<
    State the condition under which this result would be wrong, and whether you tested
    it. Name the terrestrial assumption you may have carried in without noticing:
    a fixed delay, a stationary far end, a duplexing scheme that needs slot alignment.
  >>
  EXPECT TEXT
END STAGE

STAGE INTEGRATE
  VERB INTEGRATE
  SHAPE TEXT
  ASK <<
    Which of the four attachment points did this cross, and did it stay inside them?
    If you reached for a fifth path, say so plainly — that is a contract question, and
    it is not yours to settle silently.
  >>
  EXPECT TEXT
  GATE "PROOF accepted"
END STAGE
